commit 69732e98d3ed1a6a441169748c800a559cbd92ba
Author: Travis James <travis@tribehealthsolutions.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 30 14:40:34 2026 -0500

    feat(schema-provisioning): p17-c006 phase-boundary suite — 611 passed / 0 failed with live Postgres + real keys

    The Integration-First checkpoint (5 recorded runs). Run 1 caught a real
    generator bug: CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS fails 42501 for
    flint_provisioner even when the schema exists (no database CREATE, by D3
    design) — the generator now never emits CREATE SCHEMA (schema lifecycle is
    operator-owned; FFS-001 §4.2's create_schema example contradicts its own
    §10 and loses), and plan/apply gate on a new schema_exists() port method
    with a 409 pointing at runbook §14.

    The boundary run also became the FIRST live execution of two tests that
    main-health-2026-07-29.md documents as never observed passing against real
    Postgres — both failed for pre-existing reasons (verified identical on
    unmodified main) and were repaired: rest_router_extraction's fixture never
    granted the authenticated role anything (500 on permission denied before path
    extraction was exercised); rest_typed_columns_live_pg asserted bare
    $n::boolean casts that filters.rs deliberately avoids (documented driver
    type-check failure) — expectations corrected to the documented intent.

    New e2e (all green): two-tenant RLS isolation on a provisioned table
    (tenant B sees nothing, forged-tenant INSERT refused — the FFS-001 §9
    'test that matters most'), OpenAPI hot-swap without restart via the
    version watch channel, and the armed key-rotation revocation test
    (FLINT_OLD_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, with the manual rotation procedure documented).
    Coverage gate WIRED: moved to the integration CI job so DATABASE_URL-gated
    tests count toward the 90% changed-crate threshold. fmt + clippy pedantic
    workspace clean.

